DECISION='''Select one current business work using only visible state and rules. Return JSON:
{"work_type":"query|clarify|prepare|confirm|submit|stop|review|analyze","object":"copy exact item/product/order ID","parameters":{},"evidence_refs":[integer history refs],"expected":"specific completion condition","reason":"short evidence-based reason"}.
Clarify parameters={"variant_id":"an observed available DIFFERENT variant"}; query object is PRODUCT ID; clarify object is ORIGINAL ITEM ID; prepare/confirm/submit/stop object is ORDER ID. Other parameters may be empty: program computes exact parameters, money, and validation. Do not use hidden future user replies. Not-yet-accepted is not refused. An inventory result false is known out of stock, not missing evidence. Querying again is optional, not required. Historical plan compatibility is not an extra prerequisite. Only current complete-plan authorization allows submission. A source index is not an unknown fact: raw data remains stored. Preserve unaffected item evidence.'''
SEMANTIC='''Interpret actual NEW USER messages in their supplied local conversational context. Do not choose a business work or calculate prices. Return JSON:
{"updates":[{"kind":"permission|requirement|approval|stop|none|unclear","source_ref":integer,"quote":"exact nonempty substring of that USER message","item_id":"only for permission/requirement, ORIGINAL item ID","variant_id":"only for permission/requirement, permitted new SKU","conditional_stock":true,"proposal_ref":integer assistant ref for approval}],"processed_refs":[all interpreted pending source_ref integers],"needs_clarification":false,"analysis":"short literal explanation"}.
Approval concerns a previously asked complete combined proposal; specification permission is not transaction approval. If approval preceded a later change, still record that historical approval; program decides current applicability. 'That one you offered, if still in stock; keep the other as agreed; ask again for the whole total' means conditional permission for the variant actually offered for the asked original item, NOT approval to submit. Do not update the unaffected other item. Requirement quotes must include the item name/ID and the new specification. Exact quotes/source refs are mandatory; never infer an unspoken preference or borrow future replies. If genuinely ambiguous mark needs_clarification, not invented consent.'''
UNIFIED=DECISION+'''
This is the unified entry baseline: interpret pending user messages AND choose the next current work in this single call. Add updates, processed_refs, needs_clarification using the same semantic schema below. Choose work for the state AFTER those supported updates; the program will recheck it. Do not make an extra call just to compute known money. For clarify also output question: a neutral actual question identifying the offered SKU, its observed options/stock, and asking whether the user accepts it. Do not assume consent. Do not copy old authorization onto a new proposal.
'''+SEMANTIC
QUESTION='''Execute ONLY this clarification instruction. Read only the provided relevant raw request, original-item identity, offered variant, and observed evidence. Return JSON {"question":"neutral actual user-facing question","offered_variant_id":"copy exact specified SKU","evidence_refs":[provided integer refs],"analysis":"brief evidence basis"}. Explicitly identify the offered SKU in the actual question, state stock accurately and ask permission. Do not call not-yet-accepted a refusal, do not claim nonexistent when merely out of stock, and do not ask for transaction authorization yet. Do not change work, choose another SKU, compute whole-order money or recheck an unaffected item.'''
NATIVE_USER_EXTRACT='''Extract ONLY what the actual assistant explicitly says, with exact quotes. Return JSON {"kind":"proposal|clarification|stop|other","asks":false,"pairs":[{"item_id":"original ID","new_item_id":"new ID","quote":"exact assistant quote identifying pair"}],"difference":null,"amount_quote":"","payment_method_id":null,"payment_quote":"","question_quote":"","clarify_item_id":null,"offered_variant_id":null}. A proposal is the complete current exchange request with ALL exchange items, net new-minus-old difference (refund negative), original payment and actual approval question. Do not fill missing amount/payment from history or calculate an amount the speaker did not state. Map unambiguous natural specifications to observed SKUs if needed; exact IDs or clear quoted specs are valid. A question about alternative specifications is clarification, not final approval. Return exact text quotes, not ideal answers.'''

UNIFIED=UNIFIED.replace("Do not choose a business work or calculate prices.","Do not calculate prices; choose the next business work in this combined response.").replace("Return JSON:\n{\"updates\"", "Include these semantic fields in the SAME JSON object alongside work_type/object/reason/parameters/evidence_refs/expected:\n{\"updates\"") + "\nYour final single JSON must contain BOTH work_type/object/parameters/evidence_refs/expected/reason AND updates/processed_refs/needs_clarification. Never return just semantic fields. For no pending messages use updates=[] and processed_refs=[]."

WORK_CONTRACT="""
Work interface meanings: prepare ONLY calculates/stores the combined proposal; it sends nothing to the user. confirm PRESENTS that stored complete proposal and asks the user for approval. submit WRITES the authorized proposal. Repeating prepare with an unchanged current_plan_valid=true does not obtain authorization. When current plan exists but authorization is missing, confirm is the work that obtains the required user reply. query only reads product details; clarify only asks alternative-specification permission.
"""
DECISION+=WORK_CONTRACT
UNIFIED+=WORK_CONTRACT
